<<~ ahu slot=`#/head`>>

! realm.invite.takes ~ take ~ keep a carried invite

`lares walk take <lar-invite:…>` keeps a carried invite; this vessel's hearth dial walks in on it as the face named (else the one face standing open), at once where a dial stands, else when the vessel next stands. A take for a second hearth refuses aloud and writes nothing. The walker route ships shut by name: the invite stays kept, and no hearth gate seats the walk until a live grant reader opens the route.

<<~/ahu>>

<<~ ahu slot=`#/shows`>>

!! shows ~ take

```memetic-wikitext
<<has entity=`example` name=`take` params=`invite/lar-invite:<carried> ~ keep the carried invite`>>
```

<<~/ahu>>

<<~ ahu slot=`#/takes`>>

!! takes ~ face · invite

<<~ kahea uri=`lar:///ha.ka.ba/lares/api/pono/affordance#/takes/face`>>

```memetic-wikitext
<<has entity=`arg` name=`invite` params=`takes/invite needs/required seat/1 as/<invite> ~ the carried lar-invite: string`>>
```

<<~/ahu>>

<<~ ahu slot=`#/gate`>>

!! gate ~ custody

Testimony: the door checks; this slot grants nothing.

```memetic-wikitext
<<has entity=`gate` name=`custody` params=`who/seat-or-hand ~ one sealed act frame on the custody door under the vessel key; the walk record never rests in the clear`>>
```

<<~/ahu>>

<<~ ahu slot=`#/refuses`>>

!! refuses ~ usage · refused · error

```memetic-wikitext
<<has entity=`refusal` name=`usage` params=`cure/[[realm.invite.takes invite/lar-invite:<carried>]] ~ no carried invite named`>>
<<has entity=`refusal` name=`refused` params=`~ the custody door refused the act; the message names why`>>
<<has entity=`refusal` name=`error` params=`~ the act failed outside the door's refusals`>>
```

<<~/ahu>>

<<~ ahu slot=`#/answers`>>

!! answers ~ taken

```memetic-wikitext
<<has entity=`band` name=`taken` params=`exit/0 fields/[[gatePubKey nexusAid relay leaf dialing via]] ~ the hearth, the Nexus, the leaf, and whether the dial walks now`>>
```

<<~/ahu>>

